From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:42:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: Don't set the USB state while an Alternate
 Mode is active

ucsi_partner_change() puts the port in the USB state whenever the
partner flags report USB. A partner can report USB and an Alternate Mode
at the same time, for example DisplayPort with two lanes left for USB3.
Setting the USB state then overrides what the Alternate Mode driver has
programmed into the muxes, switches and retimers, and the DisplayPort
lanes can be lost on a partner change.

When typec_set_mode() was added here, the USB state was set only when
USB was the sole partner flag, so that the Alternate Mode handlers keep
control of the mux. The conversion to bitmap accessors turned that
equality test into a test of the USB bit alone. Skip the USB state again
when the partner reports an active Alternate Mode.

This affects every UCSI platform with Alternate Mode support.

Fixes: 226ff2e681d0 ("usb: typec: ucsi: Convert connector specific commands to bitmaps")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index a5479e48859..3205877d150 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1356,7 +1356,9 @@ static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_MODE_AUDIO);
 			break;
 		default:
-			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB))
+			/* USB and an Alternate Mode can be active together. */
+			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB) &&
+			    !UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE))
 				typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB);
 		}
 
